{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human","id":1122620,"title":"Changing an inorganic being into a human","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T23:33:00-07:00","id":1122620,"title":"Changing an inorganic being into a human","content":"Hello. What kinds of spells and Arcana would be needed to transform an inorganic being, such as a robot for example, into a living human? With or without a soul would be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T23:43:07-07:00","id":1122623,"title":"","content":"Let me point you instead towards the game that's entirely about turning inorganic beings into humans...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T23:52:41-07:00","id":1122624,"title":"","content":"You can create a human from nothing with 5 dots of Life, giving them 'a true mind' with 5 dots of Mind. It's in the spell Create Life, p153. They don't have a soul, but you could give them one with Death.<br /> <br /> If you were making them from inorganic matter, you would need to put Matter in there, too, but I think you could lower it to Life 4, since you're not making it from scratch. Stone to Flesh was suggested as a Life and Matter 4 spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-30-2017, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T00:00:22-07:00","id":1122628,"title":"","content":"Basic Matter + Life Patterning should do it for just turning a conscious inorganic being into a conscious organic being for the duration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human?p=1122623#post1122623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me point you instead towards the game that's entirely about turning inorganic beings into humans...</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the very concrete feeling telling somebody to go to Promethean to run a basic Powerful Sorcery Effect is attempting to save the wrong sort of effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T00:10:59-07:00","id":1122634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human?p=1122628#post1122628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basic Matter + Life Patterning should do it for just turning a conscious inorganic being into a conscious organic being for the duration.<br /> <br /> I get the very concrete feeling telling somebody to go to Promethean to run a basic Powerful Sorcery Effect is attempting to save the wrong sort of effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that maybe it shouldn't just be a spell you toss out there, because there's a place for created humans in the CofD world already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T02:49:33-07:00","id":1122659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human?p=1122634#post1122634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm saying that maybe it shouldn't just be a spell you toss out there, because there's a place for created humans in the CofD world already.</div> </div> </div> </div>...that isn't really going to do me any good if I'm playing a mage. And when it comes to the world of darkness there are many different ways of doing similar things. For example, some prometheans are robots, but I highly doubt all robots are prometheans. And stuff that prometheans use to become human probably wouldn't help an inorganic being without any alchemy, or any of the other traits of a promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T09:53:33-07:00","id":1122728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human?p=1122624#post1122624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can create a human from nothing with 5 dots of Life, giving them 'a true mind' with 5 dots of Mind. It's in the spell Create Life, p153. They don't have a soul, but you could give them one with Death.<br /> <br /> If you were making them from inorganic matter, you would need to put Matter in there, too, but I think you could lower it to Life 4, since you're not making it from scratch. Stone to Flesh was suggested as a Life and Matter 4 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I am mistaken, you'd have to steal a soul from somebody else though, since Death can't make souls though. So Matter 4 + Life 4 to change it from a robot into a fleshy body, Mind 5 to give it a mind, and then Death 3 to steal a soul (I recommend a Sleepwalker's) and shove it into the freshly minted body (<i>Sever Soul</i> + <i>Soul Jar</i>)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And sure, Promethean covers inorganic begins trying to become actual humans, but that doesn't preclude other ways of making people, especially since this process is one <i>Supernal Dispellation </i>away from being a messy situation (because as a GM, I definitely wouldn't let this be Lasting). Not to mention if the focus of the game is the created being(s), then sure Promethean might be a better choice, but if it is the Mage(s), then this route definitely works. Hubristic, and potentially a slippery slope into Reaper-hood (if you are giving your creations souls), but doable.<br /> <br /> Plus, I could see that the Mage's quest (or dare I say... Obsession) to make their creations more permanent resulting in one of the Created being born, potentially prompting a crossover chronicle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T10:03:30-07:00","id":1122730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human?p=1122728#post1122728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, I could see that the Mage's quest (or dare I say... Obsession) to make their creations more permanent resulting in one of the Created being born, potentially prompting a crossover chronicle!</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't kept up to date with the latest edition of Promethean, but last I heard the demiurge cannot be a mage. For some reason the Divine Fire can be wielded only by mortal inspiration, not Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> You could ignore that if you wanted, but perhaps the more interesting take would be that their research somehow spills over and some mortal associate of theirs ends up becoming a demiurge instead. The fact that a mortal manages to do something the mage cannot ought to be a suitably dramatic blow to their ego.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T10:24:12-07:00","id":1122738,"title":"","content":"Ok, making a soulless human simulacrum is well and good for any old master of Life, Mind, and Matter. But if you want to make a true human with a soul from scratch, you need to be an Archmaster. Period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-30-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T10:43:51-07:00","id":1122740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human?p=1122730#post1122730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't kept up to date with the latest edition of Promethean, but last I heard the demiurge cannot be a mage. For some reason the Divine Fire can be wielded only by mortal inspiration, not Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> You could ignore that if you wanted, but perhaps the more interesting take would be that their research somehow spills over and some mortal associate of theirs ends up becoming a demiurge instead. The fact that a mortal manages to do something the mage cannot ought to be a suitably dramatic blow to their ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Mage can make a Promethean - there's one in a supplement somewhere, who I think was named the Page of Cups? - but rather a Mage cannot make a Promethean with Supernal magic. All the Divine Fire truly reaponds to is the all-consuming ibsession to create.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T10:53:40-07:00","id":1122744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122620-changing-an-inorganic-being-into-a-human?p=1122728#post1122728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I am mistaken, you'd have to steal a soul from somebody else though, since Death can't make souls though. So Matter 4 + Life 4 to change it from a robot into a fleshy body, Mind 5 to give it a mind, and then Death 3 to steal a soul (I recommend a Sleepwalker's) and shove it into the freshly minted body (<i>Sever Soul</i> + <i>Soul Jar</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're right. You need bigger magic to make a soul from scratch, but stealing souls isn't exactly difficult. You could hunt down a reaper and heroically defeat them and then take all the souls they've harvested and put them to good use without having to actually reap anyone yourself.<br /> <br /> Mages can make Prometheans but it would probably be seen as a failure of sorts. There's an example homunculus in the Night Horrors book who is an immortal magic man-golem but doesn't suffer the same problems as a Promethean would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-30-2017, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}